  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/ammocryptocharax-elegans-4/",
      "html": "<p>Ammocryptocharax elegans is a ground tetra about 4-5 cm long with a striking, intense green body colour. It can change colour extremely quickly.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/ammocryptocharax-elegans-4/",
      "html": "<p>The species was imported in small numbers from the Orinoco drainage (Colombia/Venezuela).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/ammocryptocharax-elegans-4/",
      "html": "<p>Keep the animals in planted aquariums. Only if they can sit on plants do they stay permanently green, as field studies have found.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/ammocryptocharax-elegans-4/",
      "html": "<p>The fish have an extreme ability to change colour. If they sense danger, they instantly camouflage themselves brown.</p>"
    }
